4. How do cultural and historical counting systems (e.g., Roman numerals, Mayan numerals) compare in their ability to support high number mathematics?  
5. What are the educational implications of fostering early counting skills for long-term mathematical proficiency?  

These queries and questions aim to deepen the understanding of how counting systems evolved into the frameworks that underpin high number mathematics, while exploring cognitive, cultural, and educational dimensions.  
